# L §5.13 rest largest: "each raw_j is rounded toward zero to u (down). The |total − Σ|/u leftover units, each of the
# total's sign, go one each to the keys with the largest remainders |raw_j − share_j|, so a negative total's shares are
# the negatives of its absolute value's". -100.00 PLN by 1:1:1: 100.00 splits 33.33 each and the one leftover unit
# goes to a1 by ties by pos(i) (all three tie): -33.34, -33.33, -33.33. Step 1: "A key k that the binding leaves out
# (its where false) has share 0": inc[a3] is false, so a3's share is 0 and a1, a2 split 100.00 PLN 1:1, 50.00 each.
# (Writer 6: both were REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.13.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index parts = [a1, a2, a3]
input tot: money PLN
input neg: money PLN
input w[j in parts]: num
input inc[j in parts]: bool
input hm: rounding
def sg[j in parts]: money PLN = prorata(neg, w[i] for i in parts, j, minor(PLN), rest largest ties by pos(i)) at reader
def so[j in parts]: money PLN = prorata(tot, w[i] for i in parts where inc[i], j, minor(PLN), hm, rest none) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  tot = 100.00 PLN
  neg = -100.00 PLN
  w[a1] = 1
  w[a2] = 1
  w[a3] = 1
  inc[a1] = true
  inc[a2] = true
  inc[a3] = false
  hm = half-even

ask a: sg[j], so[j] for j in parts law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a (j = a1): (-33.34 PLN, 50.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
a (j = a2): (-33.33 PLN, 50.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
a (j = a3): (-33.33 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
